Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 16:36:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 319/322] www: PPPoE baby-jumbo MTU fix in the MULTISERVICE_WAN
 WAN page (the variant that actually ships)

Field report (v2.1.4): PPPoE MTU still capped at 1492 after a factory reset;
boxes flashed over stock/Merlin kept nvram wan_pppoe_mtu=1500 and were fine.

Root cause: de6ac2d2e0 (v2.1.3) raised the caps in www/Advanced_WAN_Content.asp,
but on RTCONFIG_MULTISERVICE_WAN builds the www Makefile (line ~298) copies
sysdep/FUNCTION/MULTISERVICE_WAN/Advanced_WAN_Content.asp OVER that page at
install, so the shipped GUI never got the fix - the v2.1.4 staged fs still
carries the 1492 validator. The fix landed in the copy that does not ship.

Mirror the fix in the shipped variant, all three input paths:
- pppoe mtu/mru component checks + legacy validForm: 128-1492 -> 128-1500
- wan_mtu component check + legacy validForm: 1280-1500 -> 1280-1508
- hint texts updated to match
- BOTH silent pppoe_mtu = wan_mtu-8 clamps (new-UI applyData + legacy
  validForm) now fire only when the user deliberately LOWERED wan_mtu below
  1500; an RFC 4638 pppoe mtu (>1492) with wan_mtu at the 1500 default is no
  longer knocked back to 1492 (rc/wan.c raises the parent to pppoe_mtu+8).

Defaults unchanged (1492/1500) - opt-in as before. METAL-TEST OWED on a live
PPPoE line. Lesson for every future www fix: check the www Makefile for a
sysdep/FUNCTION variant that overwrites the base page before declaring a GUI
fix shipped.
